  </subsection>


  <subsection xml:id="subsec-bessel-second">
    <title>Bessel Functions of the Second Kind</title>

    <p>
      Above we mentioned that <m>J_{-\nu}</m> is a solution to <xref ref="eq-bessel-eqn"/>, however, the function
      <men xml:id="eq-bessel-second">
        Y_{\nu}(x) = \frac{J_{\nu}(x) \cos (\nu \pi) - J_{-\nu}(x)}{\sin(\nu \pi)}
      </men>
      is generally used instead and is called the <term>Bessel function of the second kind</term>.
    </p>

    <example>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Show that <xref ref="eq-bessel-second"/> satisfies <xref ref="eq-bessel-eqn"/>.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <solution>
        <p>
          We can write <m>Y_{\nu}(x)</m> as the power series
          <me>
            Y_{\nu}(x) = \frac{\cos(\nu \pi)}{\sin(\nu \pi)} \frac{x^{\nu}}{2^{\nu}} \sum_{m=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^m}{4^m m! \Gamma( m+\nu+1)} x^{2m} - \frac{1}{\sin(\nu \pi)}\frac{x^{-\nu}}{2^{-\nu}} \sum_{m=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^m}{4^m m! \Gamma( m-\nu+1)} x^{2m}
          </me>
        </p>
      </solution>
    </example>
  </subsection>
</section>